WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.497 --> 00:00:09.297
So before you buy

2
00:00:09.337 --> 00:00:10.417
one more ad,

3
00:00:10.857 --> 00:00:11.797
build the path.

4
00:00:12.137 --> 00:00:13.057
That’s Conversion.

5
00:00:13.697 --> 00:00:14.777
Weeks two to four.

6
00:00:14.977 --> 00:00:16.537
It’s built to turn people who look

7
00:00:16.577 --> 00:00:17.917
into people who buy.

8
00:00:18.197 --> 00:00:19.237
You leave with a brand

9
00:00:19.277 --> 00:00:20.477
that’s ready to sell.

10
00:00:20.737 --> 00:00:21.717
Take Oriva.

11
00:00:22.097 --> 00:00:22.917
New name,

12
00:00:22.957 --> 00:00:23.647
new look.

13
00:00:23.687 --> 00:00:24.557
Café owners

14
00:00:24.597 --> 00:00:25.457
still look around,

15
00:00:25.497 --> 00:00:26.737
and leave.

16
00:00:26.997 --> 00:00:28.137
So the founders boosted

17
00:00:28.177 --> 00:00:28.997
their posts.

18
00:00:29.637 --> 00:00:30.677
Visits doubled.

19
00:00:31.537 --> 00:00:32.477
Orders didn’t move.

20
00:00:32.877 --> 00:00:34.377
You’d think they need more visitors.

21
00:00:34.897 --> 00:00:35.797
They don’t.

22
00:00:35.837 --> 00:00:37.157
They need the ones they have

23
00:00:37.197 --> 00:00:37.997
to buy.

24
00:00:38.265 --> 00:00:39.885
So the website comes first:

25
00:00:40.265 --> 00:00:40.925
a salesperson

26
00:00:40.965 --> 00:00:42.305
that works all day.

27
00:00:42.504 --> 00:00:43.604
The founders wanted it

28
00:00:43.644 --> 00:00:45.284
to open with their story.

29
00:00:45.644 --> 00:00:46.424
Here’s the thing:

30
00:00:46.804 --> 00:00:48.104
a café owner doesn’t care

31
00:00:48.144 --> 00:00:49.224
about you yet.

32
00:00:49.264 --> 00:00:49.944
So it opens

33
00:00:49.984 --> 00:00:51.244
with what they get:

34
00:00:51.644 --> 00:00:52.304
beans roasted

35
00:00:52.344 --> 00:00:53.524
the week you order.

36
00:00:53.864 --> 00:00:54.644
Then proof,

37
00:00:55.164 --> 00:00:56.104
then one offer,

38
00:00:56.444 --> 00:00:57.484
and one button.

39
00:00:57.824 --> 00:00:58.724
A stranger gets it

40
00:00:58.764 --> 00:00:59.664
in under a minute.

41
00:01:00.025 --> 00:01:01.785
But nobody signs a supply deal

42
00:01:01.825 --> 00:01:03.085
off one page.

43
00:01:03.485 --> 00:01:04.685
One café owner calls,

44
00:01:04.725 --> 00:01:06.185
with three questions.

45
00:01:06.665 --> 00:01:07.385
Who are you?

46
00:01:07.605 --> 00:01:08.665
Can I see it?

47
00:01:08.705 --> 00:01:09.465
Why switch?

48
00:01:09.925 --> 00:01:11.725
The company profile says who.

49
00:01:12.085 --> 00:01:12.725
The launch video

50
00:01:12.765 --> 00:01:14.385
and photos show it.

51
00:01:14.605 --> 00:01:16.365
The pitch deck makes the case.

52
00:01:16.665 --> 00:01:17.605
She books a meeting.

53
00:01:17.965 --> 00:01:19.665
But how many never got that far?

54
00:01:19.988 --> 00:01:20.688
You can’t fix

55
00:01:20.728 --> 00:01:22.368
what you can’t see.

56
00:01:22.408 --> 00:01:23.408
So the funnel counts

57
00:01:23.448 --> 00:01:24.528
every step.

58
00:01:25.002 --> 00:01:26.009
A thousand visit.

59
00:01:26.204 --> 00:01:27.594
Thirty enquire.

60
00:01:27.634 --> 00:01:29.009
Twelve sign.

61
00:01:29.409 --> 00:01:30.889
Where did the other eighteen go?

62
00:01:31.209 --> 00:01:32.089
Look at the dates.

63
00:01:32.509 --> 00:01:33.749
Most waited three days

64
00:01:33.789 --> 00:01:34.869
for a reply.

65
00:01:35.229 --> 00:01:35.709
By then,

66
00:01:35.749 --> 00:01:37.389
they’d signed with someone faster.

67
00:01:37.889 --> 00:01:39.089
So now quotes go out

68
00:01:39.129 --> 00:01:40.169
the same day,

69
00:01:40.209 --> 00:01:41.909
and follow ups send themselves,

70
00:01:41.949 --> 00:01:43.609
to the people who asked.

71
00:01:44.089 --> 00:01:45.549
Same thousand visitors.

72
00:01:45.989 --> 00:01:46.989
For Oriva,

73
00:01:47.029 --> 00:01:48.929
eighteen now sign.

74
00:01:49.319 --> 00:01:50.539
But strangers look you up

75
00:01:50.579 --> 00:01:51.659
before they call.

76
00:01:51.959 --> 00:01:53.499
So PR takes Oriva’s story

77
00:01:53.539 --> 00:01:54.359
to the press.

78
00:01:54.703 --> 00:01:55.743
The Daily Brew runs

79
00:01:55.783 --> 00:01:56.703
the story.

80
00:01:57.123 --> 00:01:58.083
At a coffee fair,

81
00:01:58.303 --> 00:01:59.223
people taste it.

82
00:01:59.443 --> 00:02:00.283
And the social pages

83
00:02:00.323 --> 00:02:01.403
match the site.

84
00:02:01.823 --> 00:02:03.623
That’s trust ads can’t buy.

85
00:02:03.923 --> 00:02:05.623
But news lasts a day.

86
00:02:06.023 --> 00:02:06.823
What does Oriva say

87
00:02:06.863 --> 00:02:07.643
next week?

88
00:02:07.903 --> 00:02:09.623
So content runs on a system.

89
00:02:10.003 --> 00:02:10.623
Good intentions

90
00:02:10.663 --> 00:02:11.963
don’t publish.

91
00:02:12.503 --> 00:02:13.343
Calendars do.

92
00:02:13.548 --> 00:02:15.048
The founders sat down to post,

93
00:02:15.088 --> 00:02:16.228
and had nothing

94
00:02:16.268 --> 00:02:17.228
to say.

95
00:02:17.668 --> 00:02:19.048
Now one calendar plans

96
00:02:19.088 --> 00:02:19.888
what gets made,

97
00:02:19.928 --> 00:02:20.968
and when.

98
00:02:21.288 --> 00:02:21.728
Every Monday,

99
00:02:21.768 --> 00:02:23.348
they film one video.

100
00:02:23.628 --> 00:02:24.908
It becomes a reel,

101
00:02:24.948 --> 00:02:25.668
a post,

102
00:02:25.708 --> 00:02:26.108
a blog

103
00:02:26.148 --> 00:02:27.208
and a newsletter.

104
00:02:27.688 --> 00:02:28.268
One idea,

105
00:02:28.308 --> 00:02:29.908
in five places.

106
00:02:30.340 --> 00:02:31.340
Three weeks.

107
00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:33.420
Here’s what Oriva walks out with.

108
00:02:33.640 --> 00:02:35.160
So, what couldn’t they find?

109
00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:36.320
The next step.

110
00:02:36.580 --> 00:02:38.200
Nobody had shown them one.

111
00:02:38.240 --> 00:02:39.000
And the ads?

112
00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:40.140
Not yet.

113
00:02:40.600 --> 00:02:41.340
Same visitors,

114
00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:42.500
more buyers.

115
00:02:43.020 --> 00:02:43.580
Fix the path

116
00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:45.020
before you pay for traffic,

117
00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:46.500
or you’re paying people

118
00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:47.200
to leave.

119
00:02:47.526 --> 00:02:48.626
Now an ad is worth

120
00:02:48.666 --> 00:02:49.626
paying for.

121
00:02:49.946 --> 00:02:51.606
But how do you keep people coming,

122
00:02:51.926 --> 00:02:52.706
every month?

123
00:02:53.126 --> 00:02:56.033
That’s Engage.

